<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Bakr ibn Shaykh Umar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 1331</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Bakr ibn Shaykh Umar was the sultan of Mogadishu when the Moroccan traveller <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-battuta">Ibn Battuta</a> visited the city in 1331. Ibn Battuta described him as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> ruler who spoke both the local language and Arabic, governed with the advice of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qadi">qadis</a> and notables, and held elaborate Friday processions, giving one of the earliest detailed accounts of the court of Mogadishu.</p></div>
